00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Kung Fu Hustle (Chinese: 功夫; pinyin: Gōngfu; lit.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
'Kung Fu') is a 2004 martial arts action comedy film directed, produced and co-written by Stephen Chow, who also stars in the
leading role, alongside Huang Shengyi, Yuen Wah, Yuen Qiu, Danny Chan Kwok-kwan and Leung Siu-lung in prominent roles.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The story revolves around a murderous neighbourhood gang, a poor village with unlikely
heroes and an aspiring gangster's fierce journey to find his true self.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The martial arts choreography is supervised by Yuen Woo-ping.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film was a co-production between Hong Kong and
Mainland Chinese companies, filmed in Shanghai.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
After the commercial success of Shaolin Soccer, its production company, Star Overseas, began
to develop the films with Columbia Pictures Film Production Asia in 2002.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It features a number of retired actors famous for 1970s Hong Kong action cinema and has been compared to
contemporary and influential wuxia films such as Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon and Hero.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The cartoon special effects in the film, accompanied by traditional
Chinese music, are often cited as its most striking feature.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
Kung Fu Hustle premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 14, 2004, and
released on 23 December 2004 in China and on 25 January 2005 in the United States.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film received positive reviews and grossed US$17 million in
North America and US$84 million in other regions.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It was tenth on the list of highest-grossing foreign-language films in the United States as
well as the highest-grossing foreign-language film in the country in 2005.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
Kung Fu Hustle won numerous awards, including six Hong Kong
Film Awards and five Golden Horse Awards.

22
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
The film was re-released in 3D in October 2014 across Asia and North
America, marking the tenth anniversary of the film.

23
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, kung fu,
hip-hop, cinema on cinema, movie business.
